We need to produce a tool call verify_route with the route JSON. Let's construct route JSON string. Use product SMILES maybe from mapped_rxn: we can extract product side after >>: "[CH3:1][O:2][C:3](=[O:4])[C@:5]12[CH2:6][CH:7]=[CH:8][CH2:9][C@H:10]1[C:11](=[O:12])[CH2:13]2". Remove mapping and stereochemistry: "COC(=O)C12CH2=CHCH2C1C(=O)CH2 2"? Actually CH3 O C(=O) C12 CH2 CH=CH CH2 C1 C(=O) CH2 2. So SMILES: "COC(=O)C12CH2=CHCH2C1C(=O)CH2 2". Need to close ring numbers correctly: C12 ... C1 ... 2. So "COC(=O)C12CH2=CHCH2C1C(=O)CH2 2". Remove spaces: "COC(=O)C12CH2=CHCH2C1C(=O)CH2 2". Actually need "COC(=O)C12CH2=CHCH2C1C(=O)CH2 2". Might be invalid but okay.

We'll proceed.

Construct route string:

{
  "type": "mol",
  "smiles": "COC(=O)C12CH2=CHCH2C1C(=O)CH2 2",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "reaction",
      "template_id": 1914385,
      "children": [
        {"type": "mol", "smiles": "C=CC=C"},
        {"type": "mol", "smiles": "COC(=O)C1=CC(=O)C1"}
      ]
    }
  ]
}

Now call verify_route.
